    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-119914",
      "knowledge_point_id": "35fe6748-f040-5318-84e0-f3f76c9c7250",
      "knowledge_point": "Simplifying an Expression Using the Cotangent-Cosecant Identity",
      "problem": "$\\frac{{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta }-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta =$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the identity $1+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta ={csc}^{2}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta }-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{1+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta -{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
