    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-119904",
      "knowledge_point_id": "35fe6748-f040-5318-84e0-f3f76c9c7250",
      "knowledge_point": "Simplifying an Expression Using the Cotangent-Cosecant Identity",
      "problem": "Simplify ${cos}^{2}⁡z\\,({cot}^{2}⁡z+1).$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the identity $1+{cot}^{2}⁡z={csc}^{2}⁡z,$ we rewrite and simplify the expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡z\\,({cot}^{2}⁡z+1) & ={cos}^{2}⁡z\\cdot {csc}^{2}⁡z \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡z\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡z})}^{2} \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡z\\cdot \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡z} \\\\  & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡z}{{sin}^{2}⁡z} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡z}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡z})}^{2} \\\\  & ={cot}^{2}⁡z\\end{aligned}\n$$",
