    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-119906",
      "knowledge_point_id": "35fe6748-f040-5318-84e0-f3f76c9c7250",
      "knowledge_point": "Simplifying an Expression Using the Cotangent-Cosecant Identity",
      "problem": "Simplify $\\frac{1+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta }.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the identity $1+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta ={csc}^{2}⁡\\theta ,$ we rewrite and simplify the expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$",
