    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-65445",
      "knowledge_point_id": "240a0a0b-fb86-5760-bb2b-74275708ff77",
      "knowledge_point": "Simplifying an Expression Using the Alternate Forms of the Cotangent-Cosecant Identity",
      "problem": "Simplify $\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -1}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the following identity:\n\n$$\n{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -1={cot}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nSubstituting the above identity into the given expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -1} & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\cancel{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\cancel{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }} \\\\  & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "3{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta "
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta "
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{sin}^{2}⁡2\\theta "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "5${sin}^{2}⁡2\\theta $"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta "
            }
          ],
          "correct_value": "{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta "
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "provenance": {
        "activity_question": "question-65445",
        "kp_title": "Simplifying an Expression Using the Alternate Forms of the Cotangent-Cosecant Identity",
