      "problem": "Simplify ${csc}^{4}⁡x-2{csc}^{2}⁡x\\cdot {cot}^{2}⁡x+{cot}^{4}⁡x.$",
      "worked_solution": "First,  notice that the given expression is a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{csc}^{4}⁡x-2{csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\cdot \\,{cot}^{2}⁡x+{cot}^{4}⁡x & ={({csc}^{2}⁡x-{cot}^{2}⁡x)}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the  identity ${csc}^{2}⁡x-{cot}^{2}⁡x=1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({csc}^{2}⁡x-{cot}^{2}⁡x)}^{2} & =(1)^{2} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
