      "knowledge_point_id": "d012a04e-f802-5a26-b900-0801427073d8",
      "knowledge_point": "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring and Using Various Forms of the Cotangent-Cosecant Identity",
      "problem": "Simplify ${tan}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -\\frac{1}{{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we write the given expression as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -\\frac{1}{{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta } & ={tan}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor out ${tan}^{2}⁡\\theta $ and use the identity \n${csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -1={cot}^{2}⁡\\theta .$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta  & ={tan}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,({csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -1) \\\\  & ={tan}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={tan}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
