    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-65457",
      "knowledge_point_id": "d012a04e-f802-5a26-b900-0801427073d8",
      "knowledge_point": "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring and Using Various Forms of the Cotangent-Cosecant Identity",
      "problem": "Simplify ${sin}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x\\cdot {cot}^{2}⁡x+1.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we factor the ${sin}^{2}⁡x$ from the first two terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x\\cdot {cot}^{2}⁡x+1 & ={sin}^{2}⁡x(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the identity $1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡x(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)+1 & ={sin}^{2}⁡x({csc}^{2}⁡x)+1 \\\\  & =\\cancel{{sin}^{2}⁡x}(\\frac{1}{\\cancel{{sin}^{2}⁡x}})+1 \\\\  & =1+1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
