    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-23897",
      "knowledge_point_id": "d012a04e-f802-5a26-b900-0801427073d8",
      "knowledge_point": "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring and Using Various Forms of the Cotangent-Cosecant Identity",
      "problem": "Simplify $1+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta .$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we use the identity $1+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta ={csc}^{2}⁡\\theta ,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =[1+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta ]+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={csc}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor out ${csc}^{2}⁡\\theta ,$ and we use the identity $1+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta ={csc}^{2}⁡\\theta $ again. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta  & ={csc}^{2}⁡\\theta (1+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta ) \\\\  & ={csc}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,({csc}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\, \\\\  & ={csc}^{4}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
