      "knowledge_point": "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring the Alternate Forms of the Cotangent-Cosecant Identity",
      "problem": "Simplify $\\frac{{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -1}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the following identity: \n\n$$\n{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta ={csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -1\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above identity into the given expression, and then factoring it as a difference of squares, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -1} & =\\frac{{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -1} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1)(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -1)}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -1} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1)\\cancel{(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -1)}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -1}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
