      "problem": "Simplify $\\frac{2\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -2}{{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the following identity: \n\n$$\n{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta ={csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -1\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above identity into the given expression, and then factoring it as a difference of squares, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -2}{{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{2(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -1)}{{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -1)}{(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1)(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cancel{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -1}}{\\cancel{(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -1)}(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
