    {
      "math_academy_id": "e-3470",
      "knowledge_point_id": "35fe6748-f040-5318-84e0-f3f76c9c7250",
      "knowledge_point": "Simplifying an Expression Using the Cotangent-Cosecant Identity",
      "problem": "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\sin \\theta \\, (1 + \\cot^2 \\theta)$.",
      "worked_solution": "First, using the identity $1 + \\cot^2 \\theta = \\csc^2 \\theta,$ we rewrite the expression in the parentheses: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,(1+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta )=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot {csc}^{2}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the fact that $\\csc {\\theta} = \\dfrac{1}{\\sin{\\theta}},$ we can further simplify the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot {csc}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "difficulty": null,
      "answer_fields": [],
      "missing_source_fields": [
        "difficulty",
        "answer_fields"
      ]
    },
    {
      "math_academy_id": "e-3472",
      "knowledge_point_id": "240a0a0b-fb86-5760-bb2b-74275708ff77",
      "knowledge_point": "Simplifying an Expression Using the Alternate Forms of the Cotangent-Cosecant Identity",
      "problem": "Simplify $\\dfrac{1}{\\csc \\theta - \\cot \\theta}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Note that we can simplify this expression by transforming the denominator into a form where we can apply a known trigonometric identity.\n\nFirst, we multiply the numerator and the denominator of our expression by $\\csc \\theta + \\cot \\theta.$ This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta }{{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the identity $\\csc^2 \\theta - \\cot^2 \\theta=1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta }{{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta }{1} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "difficulty": null,
      "answer_fields": [],
      "missing_source_fields": [
        "difficulty",
        "answer_fields"
      ]
    },
    {
      "math_academy_id": "e-3473",
      "knowledge_point_id": "d012a04e-f802-5a26-b900-0801427073d8",
      "knowledge_point": "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring and Using Various Forms of the Cotangent-Cosecant Identity",
      "problem": "Simplify $\\csc x  + \\csc x \\cot^2 x  -\\csc^3x.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we factor $\\csc x$ from the first two terms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+\\operatorname{csc}⁡x{cot}^{2}⁡x-{csc}^{3}⁡x & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\,(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)-{csc}^{3}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the cotangent-cosecant identity,\n\n$$\n1+ \\cot^2 x=\\csc^2 x ,\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\,(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)-{csc}^{3}⁡x & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\cdot ({csc}^{2}⁡x)-{csc}^{3}⁡x \\\\  & ={csc}^{3}⁡x-{csc}^{3}⁡x \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "difficulty": null,
      "answer_fields": [],
      "missing_source_fields": [
        "difficulty",
        "answer_fields"
      ]
    },
    {
      "math_academy_id": "e-3497",
      "knowledge_point_id": "85555bce-debf-5165-ba6a-3c232deeeb0a",
      "knowledge_point": "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring the Alternate Forms of the Cotangent-Cosecant Identity",
      "problem": "Simplify $\\dfrac{1}{\\csc \\theta + \\cot \\theta} + \\cot \\theta.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we recall the following identity: \n\n$$\n1= \\csc^2{\\theta} -\\cot^2{\\theta}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above identity into the given expression, and then factoring it as a difference of squares, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta }+\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta }+\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta )\\,(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta )}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta }+\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta )\\,\\cancel{(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta )}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta }}+\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta )+\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
